  "full_text": "So I made my own graphics file format. Everybody has to support that. Everybody in the entire industry has to support mine. It's not like BMP. It's even more pure. I've taken all the cruft out of everything. That's the critical thing. If you start with a fresh slate, you start with a fucking fresh slate. I made it perfect. God's temple had to be perfect. So I have a new graphics format. They purposely fucked up the BMP beyond hope. And I made a new audio format. God said it has to be 88 piano key. He doesn't want death screams. He just wants like 88 piano keys. 127, he said. He doesn't want, we might as well, he said 127 specifically. I guess so down the line, bandwidth won't be wasted for the next thousand years. And he, the Commodore had the most memory of all computers at that time. Just remember that, 128 gig, everybody. Who knows what they can do with it, you know?",
